<item>
            <title>[ZEPPELIN-6114] Remove broken link for Google Analytics tracking </title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-6114</link>
                <project id="12316221" key="ZEPPELIN">Zeppelin</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;The ga-beacon link for Google Analytics tracking is broken. It is located on the &lt;a href=&quot;https://zeppelin.apache.org/docs/0.11.2/setup/basics/how_to_build.html#package&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;how_to_build&lt;/a&gt; page.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For the following reasons, we need to remove the link: &lt;br/&gt;
First of all, the broken link makes the page look poorly maintained. Secondly, ga-beacon doesn&apos;t seem to be supported anymore. Finally, the link doesn&apos;t seem intended to be on that page. Usually, it should be on the welcome page or across multiple pages. Since &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/1615/files#diff-180b6ccd4f65bde6bcd6ce9e7d6872d768d3b18c2e05f8faad36ff6279199ce1&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;this PR&lt;/a&gt; relocated the link, &#160;I think it might have been unintentional.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
